# FRONTEND (web/) settings for a production build.
#
# How to use:  copy this file to web/.env.production, fill it in, then run `bun run build:web`.
# Vite reads .env.production automatically during `vite build`. On Vercel/Netlify/Cloudflare Pages you can
# instead set the same names in the project's "Environment variables" screen (no file needed).
#
# IMPORTANT: everything starting with VITE_ is copied into the public JavaScript bundle, so anyone can read it.
# Never put a secret here (no seed phrase, no admin key). Keys that must be used from the browser (an RPC key)
# should be restricted to your website's domain in the provider's dashboard.

# Where the backend (server/) lives, as browsers see it. Must be https:// in production.
# No trailing slash.
VITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com

# Solana devnet RPC endpoint. The public one (https://api.devnet.solana.com) rate-limits, so use your own key
# from Helius, QuickNode, etc. and restrict it to your website's domain.
VITE_RPC_URL=https://api.devnet.solana.com
